#: ../../../frameworks/freedom-e-sdk_extra.rst:41
msgid "FreeRTOS settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../frameworks/freedom-e-sdk_extra.rst:0
msgid "heap_model"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../frameworks/freedom-e-sdk_extra.rst:45
msgid ""
"Available values: ``heap_1, heap_2, heap_3, heap_4, heap_5`` | Default: "
"``heap_4``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../frameworks/freedom-e-sdk_extra.rst:47
msgid ""
"FreeRTOS offers several heap management schemes that range in complexity and "
"features:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../frameworks/freedom-e-sdk_extra.rst:49
msgid "``heap_1`` – the very simplest, does not permit memory to be freed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../frameworks/freedom-e-sdk_extra.rst:50
msgid ""
"``heap_2`` – permits memory to be freed, but does not coalescence adjacent "
"free blocks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../frameworks/freedom-e-sdk_extra.rst:51
msgid ""
"``heap_3`` – simply wraps the standard ``malloc()`` and ``free()`` for "
"thread safety."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../frameworks/freedom-e-sdk_extra.rst:52
msgid ""
"``heap_4`` – coalescences adjacent free blocks to avoid fragmentation. "
"Includes absolute address placement option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../frameworks/freedom-e-sdk_extra.rst:54
msgid ""
"``heap_5`` – as per ``heap_4``, with the ability to span the heap across "
"multiple non-adjacent memory areas."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../frameworks/freedom-e-sdk_extra.rst:57
msgid ""
"More information about FreeRTOS Memory Management can be found in `the "
"official documentation <https://www.freertos.org/a00111.html>`__."
msgstr ""

